he same range. The X9 figure is the article's, not the maker's.\n- Leapmotor's Australian domain is parked, so the B05 figures and prices come only from The Driven's launch report. The MG U9 price is only in MG's configurator, so it isn't in the entry.\n- **Not added, kept as candidates:** Deepal E07 (maker page has only a placeholder price and no order statement), Hongqi E-HS9 (price \"below $150,000\", not final; deliveries from 2027-01-18), Avatr 07L/06T (expressions of interest only, due 2027), Chery E5 (no maker spec sheet could be read).\n- **Incomplete this run:** the 12-make re-check (step 2) was not done. Most maker sites returned 403, a parked domain or a TLS failure, so I marked no make as re-checked. The next run should start with Abarth, Alfa Romeo, Audi, BMW, BYD, Cadillac, Cupra, Deepal, Denza, Fiat, Ford and GAC. ROVER, BITRE (its download failed) and the Green Vehicle Guide's new-vehicle list were also not read.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","branch":"catalogue/add-u9-x9-b05-20261118","title":"[catalogue] Add the MG U9 EV, Xpeng X9 and Leapmotor B05"}
